-- Housing: Razorwind Shores (map 2736) static spawns and the data the housing scripts need.
--
-- Source: the owner's own retail captures, build 12.0.7.68887, 25 July 2026, parsed by WowPacketParser:
--   hbcd3: sessions\housing\dump_12.0.7.68887_2026-07-25_10-42-53 hbcd3_parsed.txt
--   hf1: sessions\housing\dump_12.0.7.68887_2026-07-25_11-03-11 hf1_parsed.txt
--   hled1: sessions\housing\dump_12.0.7.68887_2026-07-25_20-46-56 hled1_parsed.txt
--   erhousing: sessions\exiles-reach\dump_12.0.7.68887_2026-07-25_01-00-26 erhousing_parsed.txt
-- WowPacketParser SQL: Builds\housing-20260923\wpp\sql\*_world.sql. Every spawn comment names the capture
-- and the parsed-text line of the retail create it came from.
--
-- What is in this file:
--   Creatures and plain gameobjects on map 2736 with no CreatedBy and no SummonedBy, whose entity
--   fragments are only the plain unit or gameobject ones. The same spawn seen in several captures is
--   written once (same retail object guid, or same entry within half a yard for gameobjects, one yard for
--   standing creatures and fifteen yards for moving creatures).
--   The 55 "House - Plot N" gameobjects (577376-577429 and 582099). Retail sends them with no CreatedBy on
--   vacant and owned plots alike, and they are not GameObjects.db2 rows, so they are ordinary spawns here.
--
-- What is left out, because retail makes it per plot or per house, or the rule is unknown:
--   cornerstones 457142 (server code makes one per plot), front doors 602705 and 602706 (per house),
--   house MeshObjects and decor, ground WMOs 587581, 587582 and 587321 (they follow plot state),
--   the plot area trigger 37358 (server code makes it for owned plots), anything with CreatedBy or
--   SummonedBy (player pets, the player's own steward 249848), and creatures riding a transport that
--   WowPacketParser could not place. The steward 249848 still gets its captured template values below,
--   because spell 1250470 summons it and "My First Home" is turned in to it.
--
-- Phases: every spawn is PhaseId 0. The captures only carry the player's whole phase set at the time
-- each object was first seen (15 to 17 cosmetic phases), not the phase of each spawn.
--
-- Templates: nothing that already exists is deleted or replaced. Missing gameobject templates are added
-- from the retail query replies; existing creature templates only get narrow updates of columns that are
-- still at their empty default on the live database, guarded so a filled row is never touched.
--
-- The spawns need a map_difficulty row for map 2736, difficulty 0. The 12.1 client MapDifficulty.db2 has none;
-- 2026_13_32_03_hotfixes_housing_map_difficulty.sql adds it on the server. Without it ObjectMgr skips every
-- spawn below as an unsupported difficulty.

SET @CGUID := 13000000;
SET @OGUID := 13000000;
SET @NPCTEXTID := 13000000;

-- Gameobject templates missing on the live database, from the retail query replies (12.0.7.68887)

UPDATE `gameobject_template` SET `name`='Cornerstone' WHERE `entry`=457142 AND `name`=''; -- retail enUS name, hbcd3 template reply


